                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "9eb71524-f800-4915-a8ee-86f788565135",
                        "entry_id": "ac46734c-845c-3125-901b-0fd66a9e5b4d",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "shîʻite"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "66d59716-fcc8-3480-95ec-0b517592bd9d",
                        "entry_id": "ac46734c-845c-3125-901b-0fd66a9e5b4d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Musulman qui reconnait l’imamat d’Ali, gendre de Mahomet."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Chiisme"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "980a4dcf-9db5-4d4f-9e19-080ca095d65a",
                                "sense_id": "66d59716-fcc8-3480-95ec-0b517592bd9d",
                                "text": "Si j'ai tant insisté sur les inconséquences de la politique américaine en Irak depuis 1990, c'est qu'elles ont créé les conditions d'une guerre de religion entre chiites et sunnites, dont nous ne pouvons aujourd'hui prévoir l'issue, sinon qu'elle aura d'immenses répercutions […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f0b7583c-fc83-42d2-98a2-be8fec062272",
                                "sense_id": "66d59716-fcc8-3480-95ec-0b517592bd9d",
                                "text": "Khayyam feint la plus totale surprise. Il a pourtant bien compris l’allusion. Son prénom est celui du deuxième successeur du Prophète, le calife Omar, abhorré par les chiites puisqu’il fut un tenace rival de leur père fondateur, Ali."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e3a30fc0-6029-4804-afb1-fae1f9804cbc",
                                "sense_id": "66d59716-fcc8-3480-95ec-0b517592bd9d",
                                "text": "Redha, un chiite irakien, la psalmodie à Amman où il a fui les gangs d’Al-Qaïda qui dévastaient son quartier de Bagdad."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a4e83c61-8ef5-4fe7-ab8a-e2fb09ea9a7f",
                        "source_entry_id": "ac46734c-845c-3125-901b-0fd66a9e5b4d",
                        "source_sense_id": "66d59716-fcc8-3480-95ec-0b517592bd9d",
                        "target_lang_word": "Shi'a",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Shi'a",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a68535f-2abd-369f-84e2-9caf935408f1",
                                        "entry_id": "97dad6a9-cf96-37cf-8303-b898a5c9524e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The branch of Islam that believes that Ali succeeded Muhammad as leader, and that places emphasis on the prophet's family."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5df0cd75-1c85-40a1-a3e4-7fcecc1ebbf7",
                                                "sense_id": "2a68535f-2abd-369f-84e2-9caf935408f1",
                                                "text": "In Islam, Sunni is a more triumphant version of the faith than Shia, which stresses the importance of suffering, following the founder Ali, who was persecuted."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c0dc321-e7b7-4891-8464-0ee2dfcf7118",
                                                "sense_id": "2a68535f-2abd-369f-84e2-9caf935408f1",
                                                "text": "Shi’a is one of the two larger divisions of Islam, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1709b405-4385-4f8c-90ab-b32de4d1893d",
                                                "sense_id": "2a68535f-2abd-369f-84e2-9caf935408f1",
                                                "text": "Jordanians do not know what Shi’a is about, and it was very recently, [the] last few years, when we start[ed] being exposed to Shi’a."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d22fe9e2-9d5a-4f57-8f39-b3920dd97928",
                                                "sense_id": "2a68535f-2abd-369f-84e2-9caf935408f1",
                                                "text": "But the Shī'a was not yet a sect; there can as yet be no division of Islam between Shi'ite and Sunni."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0074612a-15be-3ad2-8bca-ae73d31ed78e",
                                        "entry_id": "97dad6a9-cf96-37cf-8303-b898a5c9524e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The followers of this branch of Islam; the Shiites."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "collective"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e482f2d8-e534-4c59-87fb-26727fab6cb0",
                                                "sense_id": "0074612a-15be-3ad2-8bca-ae73d31ed78e",
                                                "text": "Throughout the Umayyad period, the Shi'a were confined to southern 'Iraq [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Shi'a",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "208817ce-2cf7-3237-95bc-85f15b038d33",
                                        "entry_id": "6203afff-430b-3068-9765-e50de4608a3d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of Shiite."
                                        ],
